{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pushed: change 1739 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1739 (commit b8345508c9,\non merged main 2af5a4c773).\n\nLocal verification:\n- integration tier: 194 passed, 1 skipped.\n- ruff, mypy (527 files), module-size contract, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0.\n- main tier: 12846 passed, 52 skipped, 3 FAILED.\n\nThe three main-tier failures all pass in ISOLATION (10/10 when re-run together, no parallelism),\nand two are in code this change does not touch:\n- `test_plan_review_gate.py::test_dependency_file_deletion_invalidates`\n- `test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py::test_in_flight_refusal_clears_owned_pause_before_mutation[fsck]`\nThe third is one of MINE — `test_no_history_walk_runs_while_the_store_lock_is_held` — and it\nfailed in SETUP, not on its assertion: \"rebar create failed (exit 1): Error: git commit f…\".\nThat is the store-contention signature, not a claim about lock-held walks.\n\nI am not calling those flaky on one data point. A second full main-tier run is going now, and\nthis machine is under genuine load (the live full-store compaction stall is still running on the\nreal tracker — the same one that made an earlier `rebar comment` here wait 429s), which is\nexactly the condition that produces git-contention failures in temp stores. CI is the\nauthoritative check and runs on clean runners; if it reproduces any of the three I will treat\nthem as real and stop.\n\nWhat 1739 fixes: the sweep built one `git log --full-history` walk PER TICKET inside the store\nwrite lock. It now builds ONE position-keyed map for the whole run before taking any lock, so\nthe critical section holds only the SNAPSHOT write, the renames and the commit. Plus scoped\nstaging (no more `git add -A` sweeping a concurrent writer's in-flight event into the compaction\ncommit) and a mid-run re-yield so a sweep that began on a quiet store stands aside when writers\narrive.\n\nRED verified: reverting just the map threading and the scoped add fails three of the seven new\ntests, including \"no history walk runs while the store lock is held\".\n\nTwo gates caught me while implementing, both correctly:\n- the complexity ratchet flagged `compact_all_cli` as NEW debt (17 > 15). I extracted\n  `_run_sweep`, `_sweep_position_map`, `_sweep_should_yield` and `_sweep_one_ticket` rather than\n  raise the ceiling.\n- my first \"bystander\" test was hollow: the innocent ticket was itself a fold candidate, so\n  staging its directory was CORRECT and the test proved nothing. Rebuilt it as a settled,\n  already-folded ticket — the faithful shape of a quiet ticket another session is appending to."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786652291595366001,"uuid":"267edcb9-edcd-49af-accf-bbb8d14226af"}